; tap2sna.py file for Gunfright. Run
;
;   $ tap2sna.py @gunfright.t2s
;
; to create a Z80 snapshot.

https://zxaaa.net/DENIED/Gunfright%20(1985)(Ultimate%20Play%20The%20Game).tzx
Gunfright.z80

--tape-name "GUN.tzx"
--sim-load-config accelerator=speedlock

; The BASIC loader loads the first two blocks of screen data (P0 and P1) and
; the screen-copy block (SP), calls it, and then loads the game itself (block
; 0) at $6000. A 40-byte stub is then loaded at $5B80 and entered: it
; decrypts the game ($8000 bytes, two bytes at a time) using RLD,
; moves the whole game down by $0200 bytes to $5E00 and jumps to it. The
; simulation runs that stub, so stopping at the real start address ($A36D,
; reached from the DI; JP $A36D at $5E00) leaves the game decrypted at its real
; addresses with the loading screen intact.
--start 41837
